/target
# And a nested one: a test given a relative dump path (`OPENSHARD_TRACED_DUMP`,
# `OPENSHARD_FRAME_DUMP`) resolves it against the *crate* directory, not the
# workspace root, so `crates/<group>/<crate>/target/` appears and `/target` alone
# does not cover it. One such dump reached a commit before this line existed.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Tooling
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
.turbo/
# Byte-code the interpreter writes beside the helper scripts in `tools/`, one
# file per script per Python version. Nobody edits it and it outlives the
# script: a `font_multimatte.cpython-314.pyc` was still there after the
# experiment that made it had been deleted.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.db
/data/
/logs/
# Local, redistributability-sensitive renders derived from an installed client.
# Kept outside Cargo's disposable target directory so `cargo clean` does not
# erase long-running asset experiments.
/font-upscale-artifacts/
.env
.env.local

# The generated config. It holds plaintext passwords and one operator's network
# layout, neither of which belongs to anyone else. The binary writes a default
# on first run; `openshard_config::DEFAULT_TOML` is the version under review.
/openshard.toml

# Where the client's HUD was left: tabs, window geometry, scale. One person's
# screen arrangement, written on exit — see `crates/client/app/src/desk.rs`.
/client_ui.toml

# The route journal a client writes while somebody plays — every click and every
# replan, and the session before this one. Written unless the F1 window says
# otherwise, so it is here for the same reason the line above is: it is one
# afternoon's own record. See `docs/world/reference/path_journal.md`.
/path-journal.jsonl
/path-journal.prev.jsonl

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Local agent tooling: one operator's machine notes (where their reference
# checkouts and client install live). Shared policy and the portable MCP config
# are versioned.
CLAUDE.local.md
# A plugin's own session state — an iteration counter and a session id, written
# into the project directory by the tool rather than by anyone working on it.
.claude/*.local.*
# Embedding models the code-index server downloads into the working directory.
.fastembed_cache/
.skeleton/

# render's frame test writes here by default (OPENSHARD_FRAME_DUMP unset) for
# visual debugging. It is a render of the client's own map data and must never
# be committed — see CONTRIBUTING.md, "No client files. Ever."
*.ppm

# A world of ours and everything derived from it. A base set is an *import* of
# the client's map — the same rule as the line above, and 102 MiB of it on
# Felucca — the `.ospatch` log beside it is the edits made to that import, and
# the navigation artifact is a bake over the pair. All three are made by
# `openshard-map-import` and `openshard-navigation-bake` from files that are not
# ours to distribute.
*.osbase
*.ospatch
# The bake names itself after the world file it read — `openshard-navigation-0.bin`
# only when there is no world file, and `<stem>-navigation-0.bin` otherwise (see
# `openshard_movement::bake`). A 7 MiB `felucca-navigation-0.bin` sat untracked
# in the working tree because the narrow first pattern did not cover the stem.
*-navigation-*.bin
